              <h2 class="fw-bold mb-3">
                What is <span class="curve-text">Crypto Payment Gateway</span> Development?
              </h2>

              <p class="mb-3 nw-w-txt-2">
                A crypto payment gateway is the software that lets a merchant accept payment in digital assets and
                receive settlement in crypto or local currency, in the same way a card gateway lets a merchant accept
                Visa and Mastercard.
              </p>

              <p class="mb-3 nw-w-txt-2">
                When a customer chooses to pay in Bitcoin or a stablecoin, the gateway generates a unique payment
                address or invoice, monitors the blockchain for the incoming transaction, waits for the required
                confirmations, converts the amount if needed, and notifies the merchant's store or application that the
                order is paid.
              </p>

              <p class="mb-5 nw-w-txt-2">
                A cryptocurrency payment gateway removes the need for merchants to run nodes, track addresses by hand,
                or absorb price swings between checkout and settlement. It has become core infrastructure for e-commerce
                stores, iGaming operators, SaaS companies, travel platforms, and cross-border B2B payers who want faster
                settlement and lower fees than card networks provide.
              </p>

              <div class="d-flex justify-content-center justify-content-lg-start gap-2" data-aos="fade-up">
